Spec: Lock Shapes

Purpose:
  Prevent accidental modification of finalized shapes by locking them.
  Locked shapes cannot be moved, resized, rotated, or deleted until unlocked.

Owns:
  ./lock.ts
  ./lock.test.ts

Must:
  Locked shapes display a visual indicator (lock icon or dimmed appearance).
  Locked shapes cannot be moved, resized, rotated, or deleted.
  Locked shapes can still be selected (to unlock them).
  Lock/unlock is undoable via LockCommand.
  Lock state persists in project file (IShape.locked field).
  Multiple shapes can be locked/unlocked in one operation.
  Keyboard shortcut Ctrl+L toggles lock on selection.

Must not:
  Prevent locked shapes from being exported.
  Prevent locked shapes from appearing in the canvas.
  Allow other commands (move, resize, delete) to operate on locked shapes.

Depends on:
  @IShape (add locked?: boolean field)
  @useStore
  @SelectTool (must check lock before transform)

Exposes:
  LockCommand(shapeIds, locked)

Accepts:
  shapeIds: string[] (shapes to lock/unlock)
  locked: boolean (true = lock, false = unlock)

Scenario: lock a shape
  Given shape A is selected and unlocked
  When the user presses Ctrl+L
  Then shape A displays a lock indicator
  And dragging shape A does nothing

Scenario: unlock a shape
  Given shape A is locked
  When the user selects shape A and presses Ctrl+L
  Then the lock indicator disappears
  And shape A can be moved again

Scenario: delete blocked by lock
  Given shape A is locked and selected
  When the user presses Delete
  Then shape A is not deleted
  And a notification says "Cannot delete locked shapes"

Tasks:
  [ ] Add locked?: boolean to IShape interface.
  [ ] Create LockCommand class.
  [ ] Add lock check to SelectTool (block move/resize/rotate).
  [ ] Add lock check to DeleteShapeCommand.
  [ ] Add visual lock indicator in renderer.
  [ ] Add Ctrl+L shortcut to useGlobalShortcuts.
  [ ] Add Lock/Unlock button to Properties panel.
  [ ] Serialize lock state in project format.
  [ ] Add unit tests for lock/unlock command.
  [ ] Add unit tests for blocked operations on locked shapes.

Done when:
  Locked shapes cannot be transformed or deleted.
  Lock state persists across save/load.
  Ctrl+L toggles lock.
  Visual indicator is visible on locked shapes.
  All blocked operations show user notification.
